## The Numbers Don't Lie

577 food recalls have been reported this year alone, and we're only halfway through. There's a distinct uptick in Class II recalls (361), compared to 176 Class I and 39 Class III incidents. It's a worrying trend that merits attention. Galaxy RG Corp, in particular, has been busy this month, with a series of recalls tied to undeclared artificial colors in their products. This comes as no surprise, given their track record. They sit among the top 10 brands with the most recalls (10 in total), earning themselves a failing grade of F. 

## Galaxy RG Corp: A Technicolor Disaster

On June 17, Galaxy RG Corp recalled 10 products, including their Marquesita de Mango and Cheesecake de Guava. The issue? Undeclared artificial color additives like Yellow #5 and Red #40. These colors, while FDA-approved, can trigger allergic reactions in sensitive individuals. This oversight shouldn't be taken lightly: labeling isn't just a matter of following bureaucratic rules; it's a matter of consumer safety. 

## The Repeat Offender Phenomenon

Galaxy RG Corp isn't alone in its mediocrity. It's a member of the unfortunate club of 87 repeat offenders this year. Others, like Moonlight Packing Corporation and Albertsons Companies LLC, have also been flouting food safety practices time and again. Clearly, some brands have a lot to learn about accountability.

## What Can Consumers Do?

First, stay informed. Check for updates from official sources like the FDA or USDA. Second, if you have any of the recalled products from Galaxy RG Corp or other brands mentioned, return them or dispose of them properly. Third, demand better transparency and accountability from the brands you buy from. Consumers hold more power than they think.

Galaxy RG Corp's track record leaves more than just a sour taste--it's enough to make you wonder about their priorities. Safety and quality assurance should be non-negotiable. Let's hope the rest of 2026 fares better for our shelves--and our stomachs.
